WEBVTT

00:00:22.358 --> 00:00:24.377
Dad's missing I need
you to help me find him.

00:00:24.412 --> 00:00:25.605
I can't do this alone.

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:27.046
Dad's giving us a job to do.

00:00:27.081 --> 00:00:29.071
He wants us to pick
up where he left off.

00:00:29.106 --> 00:00:31.027
You know, saving people. Hunting things.

00:00:31.062 --> 00:00:34.020
This Demon killed mom and
Jess. I got to find dad.

00:00:34.055 --> 00:00:35.768
I've got to find Jessica's killer.

00:00:35.803 --> 00:00:36.601
I'm Meg.

00:00:36.636 --> 00:00:37.628
So, where are you headed?

00:00:37.663 --> 00:00:38.620
No way I'm telling you.

00:00:38.621 --> 00:00:40.985
You could be some freak.

00:00:41.532 --> 00:00:42.805
Dad.

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:46.764
<i>ust to get a glimpse
beyond this illusion</i>

00:00:46.799 --> 00:00:47.981
<i>I was soaring ever</i>

00:00:48.016 --> 00:00:50.857
1835, Samuel Colt made a special gun.

00:00:50.892 --> 00:00:53.698
They say this gun can kill anything.

00:00:54.736 --> 00:00:58.422
<i>Though my eyes could see
I still was a blind man</i>

00:00:58.457 --> 00:01:02.108
<i>Though my mind could
think I still was a mad man</i>

00:01:02.143 --> 00:01:04.881
<i>I hear the voices when I'm dreaming</i>

00:01:04.916 --> 00:01:08.244
I have nightmares. And
sometime they come true.

00:01:10.106 --> 00:01:13.502
<i>Carry on my wayward son</i>

00:01:13.537 --> 00:01:15.497
<i>There'll be peace when you are</i>

00:01:15.532 --> 00:01:18.668
You two are all I've got. But I
guess we are stronger as a family.

00:01:18.703 --> 00:01:20.642
We go after this thing, together.

00:01:20.677 --> 00:01:21.145
Yes, sir.

00:01:21.146 --> 00:01:23.703
<i>Don't you cry no more</i>

00:01:48.641 --> 00:01:49.920
Good morning.

00:01:50.611 --> 00:01:52.274
Can I help you?

00:01:53.413 --> 00:01:55.390
I kind of...

00:01:55.425 --> 00:01:57.367
I need to talk.

00:01:59.115 --> 00:02:01.363
That's what I'm here for.

00:02:03.809 --> 00:02:06.431
I've done some things.

00:02:07.664 --> 00:02:09.330
Not good things.

00:02:09.365 --> 00:02:12.169
Well, there's always
forgiveness for us who seek it.

00:02:12.204 --> 00:02:14.351
For everyone?

00:02:14.570 --> 00:02:16.661
Are you sure?

00:02:16.696 --> 00:02:18.409
I'll like to say...

00:02:18.444 --> 00:02:21.911
Salvation was created for sinners.

00:02:23.348 --> 00:02:26.402
Tell me what's on your mind.

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:31.081
Well, I've lied a lot.

00:02:31.116 --> 00:02:33.156
I've Stolen.

00:02:33.191 --> 00:02:35.161
I've lusted...

00:02:35.196 --> 00:02:38.001
And the other day I met this man.

00:02:38.036 --> 00:02:41.744
A nice guy, you know?

00:02:42.465 --> 00:02:48.448
We had a really good
chat. Sort of like this.

00:02:49.640 --> 00:02:55.237
And I slit his throat and ripped
his heart out through his chest.

00:02:55.272 --> 00:02:57.281
Does that make me a bad person?

00:02:57.316 --> 00:02:58.837
I know what you are.

00:03:00.965 --> 00:03:03.268
You can't be here.

00:03:03.303 --> 00:03:05.025
This is hollowed ground.

00:03:05.060 --> 00:03:06.534
Please...

00:03:06.569 --> 00:03:09.721
Maybe that works in the minor leagues.

00:03:09.756 --> 00:03:12.399
But not with me.

00:03:37.057 --> 00:03:39.655
You throw like a girl.

00:03:40.478 --> 00:03:42.698
What do you want?

00:03:43.146 --> 00:03:45.825
The Winchesters.

00:03:45.992 --> 00:03:49.431
I haven't spoken to John
Winchester for over a year.

00:03:49.466 --> 00:03:51.475
You're wasting you time.

00:03:51.510 --> 00:03:53.528
Even if I knew where they were

00:03:53.563 --> 00:03:55.947
I'd never tell you.

00:03:55.982 --> 00:03:58.072
I know.

00:04:48.777 --> 00:04:50.334
So, this is it?

00:04:50.369 --> 00:04:52.637
This is everything I know.

00:04:52.672 --> 00:04:55.569
Look, our whole lives we've been
searching for this demon right?

00:04:55.604 --> 00:04:57.962
Not a trace. Just nothing.

00:04:57.997 --> 00:05:00.286
Until about a year ago.

00:05:00.321 --> 00:05:02.452
For the first time I picked up a trail.

00:05:02.487 --> 00:05:03.649
That's when you took off.

00:05:03.684 --> 00:05:04.586
Yeah.

00:05:04.621 --> 00:05:08.354
The demon must have come
out of hiding or hibernation.

00:05:08.690 --> 00:05:10.567
All right, so what's
this trail you've found?

00:05:10.602 --> 00:05:14.067
Starts in Arizona. Then
New Jersey, California.

00:05:14.102 --> 00:05:16.423
House is burned down to the ground.

00:05:16.458 --> 00:05:19.110
It's going after families.

00:05:19.145 --> 00:05:20.696
Just like it went after us.

00:05:20.731 --> 00:05:22.115
Families with infants?

00:05:22.116 --> 00:05:23.136
Yeah.

00:05:23.171 --> 00:05:26.220
The night of the kid's
six month birthday.

00:05:26.655 --> 00:05:28.325
I was six months old that night?

00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:29.965
Exactly six months.

00:05:30.019 --> 00:05:35.416
So, basically this demon is going
after these kids for some reason.

00:05:36.148 --> 00:05:38.852
Same way it came for me.

00:05:39.597 --> 00:05:42.587
So, mom's death?

00:05:42.874 --> 00:05:44.440
Jessica, it's all because of me?

00:05:44.475 --> 00:05:45.342
We don't know that Sam.

00:05:45.343 --> 00:05:46.955
Oh, really? Cause I say
we're pretty damn sure Dean.

00:05:46.990 --> 00:05:49.413
For the last time. What happened
to them is not your fault.

00:05:49.448 --> 00:05:51.837
Yeah, you're right. It's not
my fault. But it's my problem.

00:05:51.872 --> 00:05:53.837
No, it's not your
problem. It's our problem.

00:05:53.872 --> 00:05:57.908
Okay. That's enough.

00:06:03.068 --> 00:06:04.862
So, why is it doing it?

00:06:04.897 --> 00:06:05.948
What does it want?

00:06:05.983 --> 00:06:08.701
I wish I had more answers. I do.

00:06:08.736 --> 00:06:11.385
I've always been one step behind it.

00:06:11.420 --> 00:06:15.060
Look I've never got
there in time to save...

00:06:20.248 --> 00:06:23.479
So how do we find it?
Before it hits again?

00:06:23.679 --> 00:06:25.647
There' re signs.

00:06:25.682 --> 00:06:27.214
Look, it took me a
while to see the patterns

00:06:27.249 --> 00:06:32.135
but days before these fires
signs crop up in an area.

00:06:32.170 --> 00:06:37.022
Cattle deaths, temperature
fluctuations, electrical storms.

00:06:37.577 --> 00:06:40.581
And then we backed and checked...

00:06:40.616 --> 00:06:43.887
These things happened in Lawrence?

00:06:43.922 --> 00:06:47.158
A week before your mother died.

00:06:49.041 --> 00:06:51.987
And in Palo Alto.

00:06:53.881 --> 00:06:56.308
Before Jessica.

00:06:56.343 --> 00:07:00.702
And these signs they're starting again.

00:07:01.086 --> 00:07:03.194
Where?

00:07:03.332 --> 00:07:06.325
Salvation, Iowa.

00:07:38.320 --> 00:07:39.385
Damn it!

00:07:39.420 --> 00:07:40.416
What is it?

00:07:40.451 --> 00:07:41.571
Son of a bitch!

00:07:41.606 --> 00:07:42.692
What is it?

00:07:43.145 --> 00:07:44.676
I just got a call from Caleb.

00:07:44.711 --> 00:07:45.962
Is he okay?

00:07:45.997 --> 00:07:49.198
He's fine. Jim Murphy's dead.

00:07:49.233 --> 00:07:51.291
Pastor Jim?

00:07:52.342 --> 00:07:54.343
How?

00:07:54.378 --> 00:07:56.442
Throat was slashed.

00:07:56.477 --> 00:07:59.157
He bled out.

00:08:01.989 --> 00:08:05.009
Caleb said they found traces
of sulfur at Jim's place.

00:08:05.044 --> 00:08:06.620
The Demon?

00:08:07.630 --> 00:08:08.971
The Demon?

00:08:09.006 --> 00:08:11.978
I don't know. Could be. He just got...

00:08:12.013 --> 00:08:15.075
He got careless he slipped up.

00:08:15.868 --> 00:08:19.287
Maybe the Demon knows
we're getting close.

00:08:19.322 --> 00:08:20.518
What do you want to do?

00:08:20.553 --> 00:08:22.886
Now we act like every second counts.

00:08:22.921 --> 00:08:25.995
There's two hospitals and a
health center in this County.

00:08:26.030 --> 00:08:28.053
We split up, we cover more ground.

00:08:28.088 --> 00:08:29.423
I want records.

00:08:29.458 --> 00:08:33.525
I want a list of every infant who's
gonna be six months old in the next week.

00:08:33.560 --> 00:08:35.521
Dad, that can be dozens of kids.

00:08:35.556 --> 00:08:37.410
How the hell are we gonna
know which one's the right one?

00:08:37.445 --> 00:08:40.051
We check them all. That's how.

00:08:40.543 --> 00:08:43.298
You got any better ideas?

00:08:44.822 --> 00:08:46.752
No, sir.

00:08:55.522 --> 00:08:56.939
Dad?

00:09:00.064 --> 00:09:02.123
Yeah.

00:09:03.667 --> 00:09:05.739
It's Jim.

00:09:06.113 --> 00:09:08.406
You know, I can't...

00:09:14.474 --> 00:09:16.638
This ends, now.

00:09:16.673 --> 00:09:18.767
I'm ending it.

00:09:18.802 --> 00:09:21.802
I don't care what it takes.

00:10:11.493 --> 00:10:12.704
Here you go, officer.

00:10:12.739 --> 00:10:13.853
Thank you.

00:10:29.957 --> 00:10:33.075
Hi, is there anything I can do for you?

00:10:33.434 --> 00:10:35.800
Oh, God, yes.

00:10:37.484 --> 00:10:40.092
Only I uh...

00:10:40.127 --> 00:10:43.044
Working right now, so...

00:11:33.237 --> 00:11:35.364
Train.

00:12:43.892 --> 00:12:45.175
Hi.

00:12:45.210 --> 00:12:49.015
Here, let me hold that. I don't
think you need that anymore.

00:12:49.830 --> 00:12:51.666
She's gorgeous, is she yours?

00:12:51.701 --> 00:12:52.333
Yeah.

00:12:52.368 --> 00:12:53.863
Oh, wow. Hi.

00:12:53.864 --> 00:12:56.832
I'm sorry, I'm Sam. I
just moved in up the block.

00:12:56.867 --> 00:12:58.291
Oh, hey. I'm Monica.

00:12:58.326 --> 00:12:58.760
Monica.

00:12:58.761 --> 00:12:59.684
This is Rosy.

00:12:59.719 --> 00:13:00.277
Rosy?

00:13:00.278 --> 00:13:02.702
Yeah. So, welcome to the neighborhood.

00:13:02.737 --> 00:13:04.242
Thank you.

00:13:04.277 --> 00:13:05.800
She's such a good baby.

00:13:05.835 --> 00:13:07.989
I know, she... I mean, she never cries.

00:13:08.024 --> 00:13:10.197
She just stares at everybody.

00:13:10.232 --> 00:13:12.336
Sometimes she looks at you and...

00:13:12.371 --> 00:13:15.206
I swear it's like
she's reading your mind.

00:13:15.414 --> 00:13:17.873
What about you Monica?
Have you lived here long?

00:13:17.908 --> 00:13:20.914
Oh, my husband and I we bought this
place just before Rosy was born.

00:13:20.949 --> 00:13:22.159
How old is Rosy?

00:13:22.194 --> 00:13:24.108
She's six months today.

00:13:25.273 --> 00:13:28.412
It's big right? Growing like a weed.

00:13:28.447 --> 00:13:30.182
Yeah.

00:13:34.618 --> 00:13:36.624
Monica...

00:13:36.985 --> 00:13:38.750
Yeah?

00:13:40.713 --> 00:13:42.087
Just uh...

00:13:42.122 --> 00:13:43.892
Just take care of yourself, okay?

00:13:43.927 --> 00:13:46.225
Yeah, you too Sam. We'll see you around.

00:13:46.260 --> 00:13:46.744
Yeah.

00:13:48.479 --> 00:13:51.077
Oh, here's daddy!

00:14:55.728 --> 00:14:57.453
What are you...?

00:15:06.170 --> 00:15:07.760
Rosy?

00:15:14.613 --> 00:15:16.525
No!

00:15:28.364 --> 00:15:30.333
A vision?

00:15:30.368 --> 00:15:32.289
Yes.

00:15:32.481 --> 00:15:35.640
I saw the Demon burning
a woman on the ceiling.

00:15:35.675 --> 00:15:38.107
Right and you think this is gonna
happen to this woman you met because...

00:15:38.142 --> 00:15:41.991
Because these things happen
exactly the way I see them.

00:15:42.026 --> 00:15:43.914
He started them as nightmares and...

00:15:43.949 --> 00:15:46.138
It started when he was awake.

00:15:46.173 --> 00:15:47.970
Yeah.

00:15:48.383 --> 00:15:51.592
It's like... I don't know,
it's like the closer I get...

00:15:51.627 --> 00:15:54.951
To anything involving the Demon
the stronger the visions get.

00:15:54.986 --> 00:15:58.045
All right, when were you
gonna tell me about this?

00:15:59.173 --> 00:16:00.592
We didn't know what it meant.

00:16:00.627 --> 00:16:05.665
All right, something like this starts happening to
your brother you pick up the phone and you call me.

00:16:06.111 --> 00:16:08.002
Call you?

00:16:08.791 --> 00:16:11.016
Are you kidding me?

00:16:11.808 --> 00:16:13.893
Dad, I called you from Lawrence.

00:16:13.928 --> 00:16:16.677
All right, Sam called
you when I was dying.

00:16:16.732 --> 00:16:20.193
I mean, getting you on the phone I got
a better chance winning the lottery.

00:16:25.548 --> 00:16:27.809
You're right.

00:16:29.760 --> 00:16:34.420
Although, I'm not crazy about this new
tone of yours, you're right. I'm sorry.

00:16:34.455 --> 00:16:35.875
Look, guys. Visions or no visions.

00:16:35.910 --> 00:16:39.055
The fact is we know the
Demon is coming tonight.

00:16:39.090 --> 00:16:42.195
And this family is going through
the same hell that we went through.

00:16:42.230 --> 00:16:43.864
No, they're not.

00:16:43.899 --> 00:16:47.260
No one is. Ever again.

00:16:53.663 --> 00:16:55.318
Hello.

00:16:55.353 --> 00:16:56.973
Sam?

00:16:57.240 --> 00:16:58.603
Who is this?

00:16:58.638 --> 00:17:02.784
Think real hard, it'll come to you.

00:17:03.647 --> 00:17:05.478
Meg?

00:17:07.778 --> 00:17:10.061
Last time I saw you,
you fell out of a window.

00:17:10.096 --> 00:17:12.044
Yeah, thanks to you.

00:17:12.079 --> 00:17:14.400
That really hurt my feelings by the way.

00:17:14.435 --> 00:17:16.116
Just your feelings?

00:17:16.151 --> 00:17:18.719
That was a seven story drop.

00:17:18.754 --> 00:17:21.287
Let me speak to your dad.

00:17:23.763 --> 00:17:25.262
My dad?

00:17:25.297 --> 00:17:26.643
I don't know where my dad is.

00:17:26.678 --> 00:17:32.442
It's time for the grown ups to
talk, Sam. Let me speak to him, now.

00:17:41.112 --> 00:17:42.954
This is John.

00:17:42.989 --> 00:17:45.425
Howdy, John? I'm Meg.

00:17:45.460 --> 00:17:47.827
I'm a friend of your boys.

00:17:47.862 --> 00:17:51.518
I'm also the one who watched Jim
Murphy choke on his own blood.

00:17:54.185 --> 00:17:56.608
Still there, John boy?

00:17:56.643 --> 00:17:57.805
I'm here.

00:17:57.840 --> 00:17:59.532
That was yesterday.

00:17:59.533 --> 00:18:02.118
Today I'm in Lincoln.

00:18:03.874 --> 00:18:07.160
Visiting another old friend of yours.

00:18:07.195 --> 00:18:10.175
He wants to say hi.

00:18:10.501 --> 00:18:12.315
John, whatever they do don't...

00:18:12.350 --> 00:18:13.871
Caleb?

00:18:15.088 --> 00:18:17.049
Caleb?

00:18:17.479 --> 00:18:19.143
You listen to me...

00:18:19.178 --> 00:18:22.512
He's got nothing to do with
anything. You let him go.

00:18:22.547 --> 00:18:25.646
We know you have the Colt, John.

00:18:25.988 --> 00:18:28.016
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:18:28.051 --> 00:18:29.732
Oh?

00:18:29.767 --> 00:18:31.414
Okay.

00:18:32.016 --> 00:18:34.581
So, listen to this.

00:18:38.450 --> 00:18:40.263
Caleb?

00:18:40.446 --> 00:18:41.509
Caleb?

00:18:41.544 --> 00:18:43.000
You hear that?

00:18:43.035 --> 00:18:44.842
That's the sound of your friend dying.

00:18:44.877 --> 00:18:46.961
Now, let's try this again.

00:18:46.996 --> 00:18:50.295
We know you have the gun,
John. Words travel fast.

00:18:50.330 --> 00:18:54.367
So as far as we're concerned,
you just declared war.

00:18:54.402 --> 00:18:58.404
And this is what war looks
like. It has casualties.

00:18:59.243 --> 00:19:01.924
I'm gonna kill you, you know that?

00:19:01.959 --> 00:19:03.735
Oh, John. Please.

00:19:03.770 --> 00:19:05.509
Mind your blood pressure.

00:19:05.544 --> 00:19:07.214
So, this is the thing.

00:19:07.249 --> 00:19:09.927
We're gonna keep doing what we're doing.

00:19:09.962 --> 00:19:11.680
And your friends...

00:19:11.715 --> 00:19:13.644
and anyone who has ever helped you?

00:19:13.679 --> 00:19:18.052
Gave you shelter, anyone you ever loved.

00:19:18.087 --> 00:19:22.426
They'll all die unless
you give us that gun.

00:19:26.119 --> 00:19:31.180
I'm waiting Johny. Better
answer before the buzzer.

00:19:31.633 --> 00:19:33.108
Okay.

00:19:33.143 --> 00:19:36.702
Sorry? I didn't quite get that.

00:19:36.737 --> 00:19:38.380
I said okay.

00:19:38.415 --> 00:19:40.915
I'll bring you the Colt.

00:19:41.246 --> 00:19:43.216
There's a warehouse in Lincoln.

00:19:43.251 --> 00:19:45.726
In the corner of Wellbasher and Lake.

00:19:45.761 --> 00:19:47.531
You're gonna meet me there.

00:19:47.566 --> 00:19:50.233
It's gonna take me about
a day's drive to get there.

00:19:50.268 --> 00:19:52.294
Meet me there at midnight tonight.

00:19:52.329 --> 00:19:53.033
That's impossible.

00:19:53.034 --> 00:19:55.995
I can't get there in time and I
can't just carry a gun on a plane.

00:19:56.030 --> 00:20:00.007
Oh, then I guess your
friends die, don't they?

00:20:01.005 --> 00:20:03.114
If you do decide to make it...

00:20:03.149 --> 00:20:05.343
Come alone.

00:20:12.541 --> 00:20:15.889
What the hell are you looking at?

00:20:16.341 --> 00:20:18.534
So you think Meg is a demon?

00:20:18.569 --> 00:20:21.163
Either that or she's possessed by one.

00:20:21.198 --> 00:20:22.338
It doesn't really matter.

00:20:22.481 --> 00:20:22.481
What do we do?

00:20:22.516 --> 00:20:24.436
I'm going to Lincoln.

00:20:24.471 --> 00:20:25.353
What?

00:20:25.354 --> 00:20:27.231
Doesn't seem like I have a choice.

00:20:27.266 --> 00:20:30.856
If I don't go, a lot of
people die. Our friends die.

00:20:30.891 --> 00:20:33.133
Dad, the Demon is coming tonight.

00:20:33.168 --> 00:20:35.433
For Monica and her family
that gun is all we've got.

00:20:35.468 --> 00:20:37.238
You can't just hand it over.

00:20:37.273 --> 00:20:39.008
Who said about handing it over?

00:20:39.009 --> 00:20:41.878
Look, besides us and a couple of
vampires no one's really seen the gun.

00:20:41.913 --> 00:20:43.401
No one knows what it looks like.

00:20:43.436 --> 00:20:46.297
So what? You're just gonna
pick up a ringer in a pawn shop?

00:20:46.332 --> 00:20:48.779
Antique store.

00:20:48.987 --> 00:20:51.345
You're gonna hand Meg a fake
gun and hopes she doesn't notice?

00:20:51.380 --> 00:20:53.435
Look, as long as it's close...

00:20:53.470 --> 00:20:55.169
She shouldn't be able
to tell the difference.

00:20:55.204 --> 00:20:57.922
Yeah, but for how long? What
happens when she figures it out?

00:20:57.957 --> 00:20:59.144
I just...

00:20:59.179 --> 00:21:02.333
I just need to buy a
few hours, that's all.

00:21:02.368 --> 00:21:05.512
You mean for Dean and me?

00:21:07.971 --> 00:21:11.783
You want us to stay here?

00:21:12.451 --> 00:21:14.732
And kill this Demon by ourselves.

00:21:14.767 --> 00:21:17.065
No, Sam.

00:21:17.100 --> 00:21:19.843
I want to stop losing people we love.

00:21:19.878 --> 00:21:24.608
I want you to go to school I
want... I want Dean to have a home.

00:21:29.109 --> 00:21:32.790
I want Mary alive.

00:21:35.724 --> 00:21:37.831
It's just...

00:21:40.137 --> 00:21:44.046
I just want this to be over.

00:22:16.014 --> 00:22:17.847
Did you get it?

00:22:30.533 --> 00:22:33.168
You know this is a trap, don't you?

00:22:35.104 --> 00:22:36.843
That's why Meg wanted you to come alone.

00:22:36.878 --> 00:22:38.297
I can handle her.

00:22:38.332 --> 00:22:41.311
I have the wholed loaded.
Holy water, mandake, amu...

00:22:41.346 --> 00:22:42.807
Dad.

00:22:42.842 --> 00:22:44.269
What?

00:22:44.765 --> 00:22:46.384
Promise me something.

00:22:46.419 --> 00:22:48.509
What's that?

00:22:48.686 --> 00:22:52.726
If this doesn't go south
just get the hell out.

00:22:52.761 --> 00:22:57.034
Don't get yourself killed, all
right? You're no good to us dead.

00:22:59.741 --> 00:23:02.621
Same goes for you.

00:23:03.697 --> 00:23:06.066
All right, listen to me.

00:23:06.832 --> 00:23:10.409
They made the bullets
special for this Colt.

00:23:10.444 --> 00:23:12.697
Only four of them left.

00:23:12.732 --> 00:23:16.374
Without them, this gun is useless.

00:23:18.059 --> 00:23:20.149
You make every shot count.

00:23:20.184 --> 00:23:21.664
Yes, sir.

00:23:23.450 --> 00:23:27.703
I've been waiting a
long time for this fight.

00:23:27.738 --> 00:23:31.956
Now it's here and I'm
not gonna be in it.

00:23:32.570 --> 00:23:35.884
It's up to you boys now.

00:23:37.794 --> 00:23:40.339
It's your fight. You finish this.

00:23:40.374 --> 00:23:42.523
You finished what I started.

00:23:42.558 --> 00:23:44.919
You understand?

00:24:05.362 --> 00:24:08.059
We'll see you soon dad.

00:24:12.208 --> 00:24:13.905
I'll see you later.

00:24:38.883 --> 00:24:40.918
Later...

00:26:03.743 --> 00:26:05.894
Maybe we can tell them
there's a gas leak.

00:26:05.929 --> 00:26:08.577
Might get them out of
the house for a few hours.

00:26:08.612 --> 00:26:12.136
How many times did that work for us?

00:26:12.336 --> 00:26:13.887
Yeah.

00:26:17.117 --> 00:26:20.828
Could always tell them the truth.

00:26:22.531 --> 00:26:23.741
Na...

00:26:23.776 --> 00:26:24.952
I know.

00:26:24.953 --> 00:26:28.029
I know, I know, I just...

00:26:28.064 --> 00:26:29.968
What's to become of these people?

00:26:30.003 --> 00:26:32.434
Sam, we only got one move
and you know it, all right?

00:26:32.469 --> 00:26:34.866
We got to wait for that Demon
to show itself and then...

00:26:34.901 --> 00:26:37.912
We get it before it gets them.

00:26:41.870 --> 00:26:44.962
I wonder what dad's doing.

00:26:46.831 --> 00:26:50.803
I would feel a lot better if
we were there backing him up.

00:26:53.090 --> 00:26:57.200
I would feel a lot better
if he was here backing us up.

00:28:33.162 --> 00:28:35.418
This is what we have.

00:28:35.920 --> 00:28:37.740
What?

00:28:38.260 --> 00:28:41.777
After all those years
we're finally here.

00:28:41.812 --> 00:28:44.430
It doesn't seem real.

00:28:45.303 --> 00:28:49.129
We just got to keep our heads
and do our job like always.

00:28:49.164 --> 00:28:52.460
Yeah, but this isn't like always.

00:28:55.241 --> 00:28:57.331
True.

00:28:58.947 --> 00:29:01.272
Dean, uh...

00:29:03.976 --> 00:29:06.418
I want to thank you.

00:29:07.473 --> 00:29:10.047
For what?

00:29:12.105 --> 00:29:14.643
For everything.

00:29:14.678 --> 00:29:16.852
You've always led my back you know.

00:29:16.887 --> 00:29:21.199
Even when I can't count on anyone
I could always count on you.

00:29:21.234 --> 00:29:23.288
And now...

00:29:23.643 --> 00:29:26.341
I don't know, I just
want to let you know.

00:29:26.376 --> 00:29:27.650
Just incase.

00:29:27.685 --> 00:29:30.115
Whoa, whoa, whoa. Are you kidding me?

00:29:30.150 --> 00:29:31.167
What?

00:29:31.202 --> 00:29:33.315
Don't say just incase
something happens to you.

00:29:33.350 --> 00:29:35.429
I don't want to hear
that freaking speech man.

00:29:35.464 --> 00:29:37.615
Nobody is dying tonight.

00:29:37.650 --> 00:29:40.723
Not us, not that family, nobody.

00:29:41.324 --> 00:29:43.575
Except that Demon.

00:29:43.610 --> 00:29:48.502
That evil son of a bitch ain't getting
any older than tonight. You understand me?

00:29:59.757 --> 00:30:01.949
John. You made it.

00:30:01.984 --> 00:30:04.106
Too bad really.

00:30:04.141 --> 00:30:06.569
I was hoping to kill
more of your friends.

00:30:06.604 --> 00:30:08.796
Sorry to disappoint.

00:30:08.831 --> 00:30:12.502
I can see where your
boys get their good looks.

00:30:12.537 --> 00:30:18.570
I must admit, considering what they
say about you I thought you'd be taller.

00:30:21.051 --> 00:30:23.823
Well, aren't you the chatty one?

00:30:23.858 --> 00:30:26.595
You want to get to business?

00:30:27.236 --> 00:30:28.939
Fine.

00:30:29.652 --> 00:30:31.591
Why don't you hand over the gun?

00:30:31.626 --> 00:30:34.593
If I give you the gun,
how do I get out of here?

00:30:34.628 --> 00:30:38.674
If you're as good as they say you are,
I'm sure you'll figure something out.

00:30:38.709 --> 00:30:40.618
Maybe I'll just shoot you.

00:30:40.653 --> 00:30:43.250
You want to shoot me, baby? Go ahead.

00:30:43.285 --> 00:30:48.327
It won't end anything.
There's more where I came from.

00:30:52.495 --> 00:30:54.061
Who the hell's that?

00:30:54.096 --> 00:30:58.435
He's not as nearly as much fun
as I am, I can tell you that.

00:30:58.470 --> 00:31:02.286
So, I suggest you give us the gun.

00:31:08.449 --> 00:31:10.786
Now!

00:31:21.044 --> 00:31:23.232
This is the Colt?

00:31:28.736 --> 00:31:31.272
What do you think?

00:31:52.569 --> 00:31:54.922
You shot me!

00:31:55.506 --> 00:31:59.089
I can't believe you just shot me!

00:32:00.321 --> 00:32:02.609
It's a fake!

00:32:12.475 --> 00:32:13.982
You're dead John.

00:32:14.017 --> 00:32:15.455
You're boys are dead.

00:32:15.490 --> 00:32:18.466
I never used the gun. How can
I know it would never work?

00:32:18.501 --> 00:32:21.443
I'm so not in the mood for
this. I've just been shot!

00:32:21.478 --> 00:32:24.371
Well I guess you're
lucky the gun wasn't real.

00:32:24.406 --> 00:32:26.164
That's funny, John.

00:32:26.199 --> 00:32:31.603
We're gonna strip the skin from
your bones but that was funny.

00:33:16.008 --> 00:33:18.561
Holy water, John.

00:33:18.596 --> 00:33:21.457
Real cute.

00:33:31.660 --> 00:33:34.241
Dad's not answering.

00:33:37.216 --> 00:33:39.133
Maybe Meg was late.

00:33:39.168 --> 00:33:40.756
Maybe the reception is bad.

00:33:40.791 --> 00:33:42.098
Yeah, well...

00:33:47.513 --> 00:33:49.715
Dean, wait.

00:33:50.599 --> 00:33:52.281
Listen.

00:34:15.309 --> 00:34:17.451
It's coming.

00:34:25.279 --> 00:34:26.832
Damn it.

00:34:54.769 --> 00:34:56.502
Get out of my house!

00:34:57.788 --> 00:34:59.522
Get out of my house!

00:35:01.482 --> 00:35:02.561
Mr. Hold, please.

00:35:02.596 --> 00:35:03.493
Be quite and listen to me.

00:35:03.494 --> 00:35:05.710
Be quite and listen to me.
We are trying to help you.

00:35:05.745 --> 00:35:06.714
Charlie?

00:35:06.749 --> 00:35:07.683
Okay?

00:35:07.684 --> 00:35:08.821
Everything okay down there?

00:35:08.856 --> 00:35:09.830
Monica, get the baby!

00:35:09.831 --> 00:35:11.007
Don't go over there!

00:35:11.042 --> 00:35:12.183
You stay away from her!

00:35:18.213 --> 00:35:20.559
What are you..

00:35:35.325 --> 00:35:36.758
Where the hell did it go?

00:35:36.793 --> 00:35:37.293
My baby!

00:35:37.328 --> 00:35:38.800
No, hey wait.

00:35:38.801 --> 00:35:40.740
Get her out of here, I got it.

00:35:41.010 --> 00:35:42.219
Come on.

00:35:42.254 --> 00:35:43.213
My baby!

00:35:43.248 --> 00:35:44.279
Dean's got her.

00:36:40.638 --> 00:36:42.623
You get away from my family!

00:36:42.658 --> 00:36:44.608
Charlie, don't. They saved us.

00:36:44.643 --> 00:36:46.255
They saved us...

00:36:54.130 --> 00:36:55.981
Thank you.

00:37:00.067 --> 00:37:01.733
It's still in there.

00:37:02.013 --> 00:37:03.128
Sam, Sam. No!

00:37:03.163 --> 00:37:04.504
Dean, let me go. It's still in there!

00:37:04.539 --> 00:37:05.845
It's burning to the
ground. It's suicide!

00:37:05.880 --> 00:37:06.714
I don't care!

00:37:06.749 --> 00:37:08.043
I do!

00:37:24.027 --> 00:37:27.889
Come on, dad. Answer
your phone, damn it!

00:37:31.494 --> 00:37:33.989
Something's wrong.

00:37:36.094 --> 00:37:38.266
You hear me? Something's happened.

00:37:38.301 --> 00:37:40.438
If you had just let me go in there...

00:37:40.473 --> 00:37:43.678
I could have ended all this.

00:37:43.713 --> 00:37:45.092
Sam...

00:37:45.127 --> 00:37:48.227
The only thing you
would end was your life.

00:37:48.905 --> 00:37:51.262
You don't know that.

00:37:51.297 --> 00:37:54.914
So what? You're willing to
sacrifice yourself? Is that it?

00:37:55.423 --> 00:37:57.665
Yeah. Yeah, you're damn right I am.

00:37:57.700 --> 00:37:59.907
Yeah, well that's not gonna
happen. Not as long as I'm around.

00:37:59.942 --> 00:38:01.451
What the hell are you
talking about Dean?

00:38:01.486 --> 00:38:04.217
We've been searching for
this Demon our whole lives.

00:38:04.252 --> 00:38:05.858
It's the only thing
we've ever cared about.

00:38:05.893 --> 00:38:08.667
Sam, I want to waste it. I do, okay?

00:38:08.702 --> 00:38:10.661
But it's not worth dying over?

00:38:10.696 --> 00:38:11.215
What?

00:38:11.250 --> 00:38:12.565
I mean it.

00:38:12.566 --> 00:38:16.035
If hunting this Demon means
you getting yourself killed.

00:38:16.070 --> 00:38:18.417
Then I hope we never
find the damn thing.

00:38:18.452 --> 00:38:21.433
That thing killed Jess.

00:38:22.335 --> 00:38:25.095
That thing killed mom.

00:38:25.563 --> 00:38:28.478
You said yourself once.

00:38:28.629 --> 00:38:31.621
That no matter what we do they're gone

00:38:31.656 --> 00:38:34.063
and they're never coming back.

00:38:34.521 --> 00:38:37.284
Don't just say that! Don't you!

00:38:37.319 --> 00:38:40.047
After all this, don't you say that.

00:38:41.629 --> 00:38:45.230
Sam, look.

00:38:45.265 --> 00:38:48.082
The three of us...

00:38:48.285 --> 00:38:51.081
That's all we have.

00:38:52.587 --> 00:38:55.611
It's all I have.

00:38:58.834 --> 00:39:03.092
Sometimes I feel like I'm
barely holding it together, man.

00:39:03.954 --> 00:39:06.846
Without you and dad...

00:39:07.820 --> 00:39:09.889
Dad...

00:39:14.975 --> 00:39:17.351
He should have called by now.

00:39:17.386 --> 00:39:19.851
Try again.

00:39:36.377 --> 00:39:40.189
You boys really screwed up this time.

00:39:43.058 --> 00:39:45.408
Where is he?

00:39:45.588 --> 00:39:48.840
You're never gonna
see your father again.



00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:07.000
